<title>AUSTRALIA: Lend Lease completes share buy-back.</title>
<headline>Lend Lease completes share buy-back.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lend Lease Corp Ltd said on Tuesday it had finalised its planned share buy-back programme by buying 1.58 million ordinary shares on the market for a total of just over A$42.1 million.</p>
<p>The shares represented 0.63 percent of the company's ordinary shares. The highest price paid was A$28 per share, and the lowest A$25.70, Lend Lease said.</p>
<p>Lend Lease shares were trading at A$27.95 at 11.00 a.m. (0100 GMT) on Tuesday, five cents down from Monday's close.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
